 "observations": [
  "col_left L1: «*aṭ-ṭarf*» is printed in italics, with the dots under both t.",
  "col_left L2: «*Ta’rīkh-i-Rashīdī*» is printed in italics, read at 8,000 dpi: the sign of the hamzah after the a is printed as a round dot (1.7 by 1.7 points, 6.1–7.8 points above the baseline), the head of the apostrophe without its tail; transcribed ’. The T has a short upright stroke at the right end of its top, as the italic T of «*Tabulae*» on p. 409; the i of «rīkh» and the second and the last i of «Rashīdī» have their bars (the last one joined to the top of the d, which is printed broken); both hyphens are printed short, the first like a point at mid height (1.7 by 1.2 points); read as hyphens.",
  "col_left L3: the accent of «sammà» is printed as a small upright teardrop (1.4 by 2.3 points), without the slant of a grave (compared at 8,000 dpi with the grave of «ǵumādà» on p. 404, which slants down to the right by 0.6 point over its height); read à, as «*sammà*» on p. 405.",
  "col_left L4: «*Tasṭīḥ aṣ-ṣuwar*» is printed in italics, with the dot under the t, the bar over the i, the dot under the h and the dots under both s.",
  "col_left L13, L16, L21, L22, L24: «*72-73*», «*95*», «*78*», «*93-94*», «*17-*» «*19*» and «*14-15*» are printed in italics.",
  "col_left L18: a speck (0.6 point) to the right of «eclipses.», 2 points above the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L23, L24: the last e of «sintne» and of «incolae» (L24) is printed broken, like c; read e.",
  "col_left L27: «Τεῦκρος» is Greek, with the circumflex on the υ; the κ is printed in its cursive form (ϰ).",
  "col_left L29: «ath-Tha‘ālibī» has the sign of ‘ayn and the bars over the second a and the last i; «Yatīmat» has the bar over the i.",
  "col_left L31, L43: «Thābit» has the bar over the a.",
  "col_left L31: the lower point of the V of «{sc:xvii}» stands apart (1.7 by 1.6 points, on the baseline), like a point; it is not a point.",
  "col_left L32: the footnote reference «(1)» after «n. 1» is printed in the type of the text, on the line.",
  "col_left L33: «(duo libelli)» is printed with a broken o; the lower feet of the small capitals of «{sc:lxxv}-{sc:lxxvi}» stand apart in places like points; none of them is a point.",
