  "col_right L43: «τροπή» is Greek, with the acute on the η, whose right leg is printed apart. The d of «trepidatio» is printed broken.",
  "col_left, col_right: the ball terminals of the 3s often stand apart from the figure, at mid height and on the baseline (like a colon before it), in «303», «310» and «319» (L39), «310» (L27), «312» (L28), «329» (R1), «263» (R11), «237» (R13), «341» (R15), «35» (R22) and «321-322» (R42); the lower balls stand low on the line like points, as do the tails of the 9s of «*19*» (L22) and the ball of the 5 of «351» (L28). loose_pieces.py lists 92 loose pieces on this page; none of them is a point.",
  "notes L1: the rule over the footnote (115.5 points long, from 272.0 to 387.5, at 736.3, under the middle of the page) lies 14.8 points below the last lines of the columns. The footnote is set in one column across the page; it belongs to «(1)» in L32 of the left column. «{sp:Björnbo}» is letter-spaced; «*Die mathem. S. Marcohandschriften*» is printed in italics.",
